<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="70827" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/ECE/598/70827.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2025" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025.xml">2025</calendarYear><term id="120251" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring.xml">Spring 2025</term><subject id="ECE" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/ECE.xml">Electrical and Computer Engineering</subject><course id="598" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/ECE/598.xml">Special Topics in ECE</course></parents><sectionNumber>PD </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Fiber Photonics</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course will not focus on the transmission of signals, as in telecommunications systems, but rather on harnessing the light-matter interactions that enable the generation, manipulation, and control of light with fiber. Topics range from mode theory, propagation, and fiber design, to fiber-based sensors and high power fiber laser systems. Prerequisites: Credit or concurrent enrollment in ECE 520, plus one of ECE 455 or 495 or ECE 572 or equivalent.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2025-01-21Z</startDate><endDate>2025-05-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LEC">Lecture</type><start>02:00 PM</start><end>03:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>2015</roomNumber><buildingName>Electrical &amp; Computer Eng Bldg</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Dragic" firstName="P">Dragic, P</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>